
# A. account.lease.grant derives share and epoch from the account row (A owner, B target, trust on)

## A1 first grant without shareId/epoch: minted share, epoch 1, persisted on the row
```json
{
  "grant": {
    "shareId": "a8250358-9dda-47ea-a4ba-d4e8b5bd8d57",
    "epoch": 1,
    "nodeId": "apiary-node-b",
    "expiresAt": 1793991691
  },
  "install": {
    "id": "codex-lx",
    "shareId": "a8250358-9dda-47ea-a4ba-d4e8b5bd8d57",
    "epoch": 1,
    "nodeId": "apiary-node-b"
  },
  "row": {
    "id": "codex-lx",
    "source": "local",
    "shareId": "a8250358-9dda-47ea-a4ba-d4e8b5bd8d57",
    "shareEpoch": 1,
    "lease": null
  }
}
```

## A2 caller-supplied share facts must agree with the row
```json
{
  "second grant, no params: same share and epoch, later window": "ok",
  "caller passes the row's own shareId + epoch 1": "ok",
  "caller passes another shareId": "invalid_request (share_id)",
  "caller passes epoch 2 (row is at 1)": "invalid_request (epoch)",
  "caller passes epoch 0": "invalid_request (epoch)"
}
```

## A3 B installs the payload: the leased row carries the same share and epoch
```json
{
  "id": "codex-lx@a8250358",
  "source": "leased",
  "shareId": "a8250358-9dda-47ea-a4ba-d4e8b5bd8d57",
  "shareEpoch": 1,
  "lease": {
    "shareId": "a8250358-9dda-47ea-a4ba-d4e8b5bd8d57",
    "epoch": 1,
    "authorityNodeId": "32b189b8-e2b6-4b64-81f2-373b93a70193",
    "expiresAt": 1794034891
  }
}
```

